 -->grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit,minmax(200px,1fr));
 ✅ repeat(auto-fit, …)
repeat() → repeats column pattern
auto-fit → automatically fits as many columns as possible in the container

👉 Difference:

auto-fit → collapses empty columns (good for responsiveness)
auto-fill → keeps empty columns (can leave gaps)

✅ minmax(200px, 1fr)

Defines column size range:

Minimum width: 200px
Maximum width: 1fr (fraction of available space)

👉 Meaning:

Each column will be at least 200px
If space is available, it will expand equall
👉 "It creates a responsive grid where columns automatically 
fit into the container, each having
 a minimum width of 200px and expanding equally using 1fr."
 🔥 Priority Order
Fit as many columns as possible using the minimum (200px)
Only after that → distribute extra space (1fr)

