📘 CSS all Property – Complete Guide
🔹 What is all?
all: value;

👉 It is a shorthand that resets or controls ALL CSS properties at once
(except a few like direction and unicode-bidi)

🔹 Possible Values of all
✅ 1. all: unset;
all: unset;

👉 Behavior:

Inherited properties → inherit
Non-inherited → initial
✔ Example
button {
    all: unset;
}

👉 Removes almost everything → clean slate

✅ 2. all: initial;
all: initial;

👉 Behavior:

Resets everything to default CSS values
✔ Example
div {
    all: initial;
}

👉 Acts like browser default styles

✅ 3. all: inherit;
all: inherit;

👉 Behavior:

Takes all properties from parent
✔ Example
div {
    all: inherit;
}

👉 Fully copies parent styling

✅ 4. all: revert; (🔥 Important)
all: revert;

👉 Behavior:

Reverts styles to browser stylesheet OR previous CSS layer
Ignores your custom CSS

-->if we have two div and first get width and for second we give 100% then it will cover all remaining area
--->🔥 Direction Difference (VERY IMPORTANT)
✅ In relative

👉 Values are like movement

Property	Meaning
top: 20px	move DOWN
left: 20px	move RIGHT
right: 20px	move LEFT
bottom: 20px	move UP
✅ In absolute

👉 Values are like distance from edges

Property	Meaning
top: 20px	20px from top of parent
left: 20px	20px from left
right: 20px	20px from right
bottom: 20px	20px from bottom


👉 All three (absolute, fixed, sticky) use top, left, right, bottom the SAME way
| Position | Reference                          |
|----------|-----------------------------------|
| static   | normal document flow              |
| relative | itself (original position)        |
| absolute | nearest positioned(relative or absolute) parent         |
| fixed    | viewport (screen)                 |
| sticky   | parent (then viewport on scroll)  |


--->disply:flex vs flex-inline
| Feature     | flex           | inline-flex   |
| ----------- | -------------- | ------------- |
| Line break  | Yes (block)    | No (inline)   |
| Width       | Full available | Content-based |
| Layout flow | New line       | Same line     |
| Children    | Flex items     | Flex items    |


-->
1. flex: 1 1 0
flex: 1 1 0;
Meaning:
flex-grow: 1 → grow equally
flex-shrink: 1 → shrink equally
flex-basis: 0 ⭐ (IGNORE content)//means all the flex-items will have equal width regardless of thier content
✔ Result:

👉 All items get exact equal width
👉 Content does NOT affect layout

2. flex: 1 1 auto
flex: 1 1 auto;
Meaning:
flex-grow: 1
flex-shrink: 1
flex-basis: auto ⭐ (content decides starting size)//means if one flex-item has more content then it will not wrap first it 
fill try to cover area that is available then all grow 
✔ Result:
👉 Content affects initial width
👉 Then space is distributed


-->inline-block elements shrink according to content unless (fixed)width is given
-->text-align: center;
only centers:
text
inline elements
inline-block elements

It does NOT center block elements like div.